 174:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** * Summary:
 175:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  Modifies the clock divider and, thus, the frequency. When the clock divider
 176:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  register is set to zero or changed from zero, the clock will be temporarily
 177:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  disabled in order to change the SSS mode bit. If the clock is enabled when
 178:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  SetDividerRegister is called, then the source clock must be running.
 179:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *
 180:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** * Parameters:
 181:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  clkDivider:  Divider register value (0-65,535). This value is NOT the
 182:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *    divider; the clock hardware divides by clkDivider plus one. For example,
 183:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *    to divide the clock by 2, this parameter should be set to 1.
 184:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  restart:  If nonzero, restarts the clock divider: the current clock cycle
 185:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *   will be truncated and the new divide value will take effect immediately. If
 186:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *   zero, the new divide value will take effect at the end of the current clock
 187:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *   cycle.
 188:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *
 189:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** * Returns:
 190:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *  None
 191:Generated_Source\PSoC5/timer_clock_3.c **** *
